# Build-hashed assets are immutable; public files without hashes must revalidate.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Invitation-only beta: ask crawlers not to list anything except the public
# pages in src/app/lib/searchIndexing.ts's PUBLIC_INDEXABLE_PATHS allowlist.
# Only matters for a Cloudflare Pages deploy (`npm run deploy`); the
# Caddy/Docker production path serves next.config.ts's headers() instead
# (docs/search-indexing.md). Cloudflare Pages joins the values of every
# header set by a matching rule, so re-declaring `X-Robots-Tag: index,
# follow` on the public paths would combine with the blanket noindex into
# "noindex, nofollow, index, follow" (the most restrictive wins) instead of
# overriding it. `!` unsets a header a more general rule set, so the public
# paths carry no X-Robots-Tag at all, same as production.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/
  ! X-Robots-Tag

/privacidad
  ! X-Robots-Tag

/terminos
  ! X-Robots-Tag
